in":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search_files 'deploy_review_bot' in autodeploy.sh -> (no matches)","Function list (lines with '() {') contains no deploy_review_bot; record_backoff_failure defined at top level :489","search_files 'record_backoff_failure' shows call sites at 631-703 inside the mcp block and at 566/569 shared paths","autodeploy.sh:510 'if changed \"$BOT_PATHS\" || changed \"$SECRETS_PATHS\"; then' — the bot logic is an inline if-block, not a function"],"finding":"The 'Scope growth / Failure' paragraph asserts the existing backoff is scoped 'to the bot (every call site is inside deploy_review_bot)'. No function named deploy_review_bot exists in autodeploy.sh — the review-bot logic is an inline top-level `if changed \"$BOT_PATHS\"` block — and record_backoff_failure is actually called from many mcp-block sites (lines 631, 634, 650, 653, 656, 664, 673, 681, 694, 703) and shared checkout/rsync failure paths (566, 569), not exclusively from a bot function.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f676cb06d80c467be","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope growth across review rounds -> 'Failure': 'every call site is inside deploy_review_bot'","norm_id":"n281e0f07f4f306c5","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementing the 'scope the existing backoff file to the bot' change on the stated assumption that all callers are inside one bot function"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace the 'every call site is inside deploy_review_bot' claim with the true call-site inventory (bot inline block + mcp block + shared checkout/rsync), and specify how each is re-scoped to per-component backoff files.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails